# AREngine M15 test fixture: a square-based pyramid, hand-authored
# directly in AREngine's own local-space convention (CCW-from-outside
# winding, uv(0,0) = local low-U/low-V corner per face - the same rule
# ProceduralMesh::AppendFace uses), so DecodeMeshOBJ needs zero winding
# reversal, axis conversion, or V-flip. The four base vertices below are
# byte-for-byte ProceduralMesh.cpp's own -Y cube face, in the same
# order, so the base triangulation is provably correct by identity with
# already-shipping rendering code, not just re-derived math. See
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, "M15 - Asset-Backed Mesh Loading Foundation".
#
# Deliberately narrow: positions (v) and texture coordinates (vt) only
# - no normals (vn), no vertex colors, no mtllib/usemtl. v1 = apex,
# v2..v5 = base corners (B0..B3).

v 0.0 0.5 0.0
v -0.5 -0.5 -0.5
v 0.5 -0.5 -0.5
v 0.5 -0.5 0.5
v -0.5 -0.5 0.5

# Base quad UVs (0,0)/(1,0)/(1,1)/(0,1) assigned to B0/B1/B2/B3 - the
# same corner-to-UV rule AppendFace uses, and deliberately reused across
# both base triangles below (vt1 and vt3 each appear in both f lines) to
# exercise real (vertex_index, texcoord_index) dedup.
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 1.0 1.0
vt 0.0 1.0

# Each triangular side face gets its own independent UV range.
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 0.5 1.0
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 0.5 1.0
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 0.5 1.0
vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 0.5 1.0

# Base (B0, B1, B2) + (B2, B3, B0) - same corner order/split as
# ProceduralMesh::AppendFace's own quad triangulation.
f 2/1 3/2 4/3
f 4/3 5/4 2/1

# Sides: (B1, B0, apex), (B2, B1, apex), (B3, B2, apex), (B0, B3, apex).
f 3/5 2/6 1/7
f 4/8 3/9 1/10
f 5/11 4/12 1/13
f 2/14 5/15 1/16
